# Ferocification, second mode: "Target creature you control gains menace and haste until end of turn" (CR 702.110, 702.10, 506.1). Memnite is cast on turn 3, before combat, so it could not
# attack; the mode gives it haste and menace. Bot2's two Ornithopters (flying 0/2) cannot block it one at a time; with two blockers declared together the block is legal. Turn 4: no trigger on
# an opponent's turn, and the keywords are gone.
[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Ferocification
Memnite
Island x4
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter x2
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Ferocification.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.BeginCombat]
Bot1.Modes(2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Keywords = Haste; Menace
? Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Power = 1
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Memnite > Bot2)
! Bot2.Block(Ornithopter#1 > Memnite)
Bot2.Block(Ornithopter#1 > Memnite; Ornithopter#2 > Memnite)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 20
? Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Damage = 0
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Stack.Count = 0

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 20
